		"name": "Notejam SCIM API - Complete Collection",
		"description": "Complete collection of the Notejam SCIM API with all tested and validated functionalities.\n\n## 📋 Included Features:\n\n- ✅ All HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE)\n    \n- ✅ SCIM filters (boolean, numeric, string, date, complex)\n    \n- ✅ SCIM pagination\n    \n- ✅ Real usage examples\n    \n\n## ⚠️ IMPORTANT:\n\nThe `customFields` field must be sent as a JSON string: `\"customFields\": \"{\\\"test\\\": \\\"value\\\"}\"`\n\n## 🚀 Step-by-Step Testing Instructions:\n\n### 1\\. Setup:\n\n- Import this collection into Postman\n    \n- Configure the `baseUrl` variable in the collection variables\n    \n- Ensure the Notejam application is running on the configured URL\n    \n\n### 2\\. Basic CRUD Testing:\n\n1. Start with \"COMPLETE DEMO\" folder\n    \n2. Run \"Automatic Demo - PADS\" to verify basic connectivity\n    \n3. Run \"Automatic Demo - NOTES\" to verify notes endpoint\n    \n4. Execute \"Individual Filter Test\" requests to validate SCIM filtering\n    \n\n### 3\\. Full CRUD Operations:\n\n1. **PADS - Complete CRUD** folder:\n    \n    - GET /pads (list all pads)\n        \n    - POST /pads (create new pad)\n        \n    - GET /pads/{id} (retrieve specific pad)\n        \n    - PUT /pads/{id} (update pad completely)\n        \n    - PATCH /pads/{id} (partial update)\n        \n    - DELETE /pads/{id} (logical deletion)\n        \n2. **NOTES - CRUD Completo** folder:\n    \n    - Follow the same pattern as PADS\n        \n    - Test all CRUD operations for notes\n        \n\n### 4\\. SCIM Filter Testing:\n\n1. **SCIM FILTERS - PADS** folder:\n    \n    - Test boolean filters (active eq true/false)\n        \n    - Test numeric filters (status eq 1/2)\n        \n    - Test string filters (name eq \"Reunioes\")\n        \n    - Test date filters (created gt \"2025-08-28T00:00:00\", modified gt \"2025-08-28T20:00:00\")\n        \n    - Test complex filters (active eq true and status eq 1)\n        \n2. **SCIM FILTERS - NOTES** folder:\n    \n    - Test similar filter patterns for notes\n        \n    - Test date filters for notes creation and modification\n        \n    - Verify text-based filtering works correctly\n        \n\n### 5\\. Pagination Testing:\n\n1. **PAGINAÇÃO SCIM** folder:\n    \n    - Test first page (startIndex=1, count=5)\n        \n    - Test second page (startIndex=6, count=5)\n        \n    - Verify totalResults count is accurate\n        \n\n### 6\\. Advanced Examples:\n\n1. **EXEMPLOS AVANÇADOS** folder:\n    \n    - Test filter + pagination combinations\n        \n    - Verify complex queries work correctly\n        \n\n### 7\\. Validation:\n\n- All requests should return appropriate HTTP status codes\n    \n- GET requests should return 200 OK\n    \n- POST requests should return 201 Created\n    \n- PUT/PATCH requests should return 204 No Content\n    \n- DELETE requests should return 204 No Content\n    \n- Check that response bodies contain expected data structure\n    \n- Verify that filters return the correct number of results\n    \n- Ensure pagination works correctly with totalResults\n    \n\n### 8\\. Troubleshooting:\n\n- If requests fail, check the application logs\n    \n- Verify the `baseUrl` variable is correctly set\n    \n- Ensure the database is accessible and contains test data\n    \n- Check that all required services are running\n    \n\n### 9\\. Expected Results:\n\n- All CRUD operations should work without errors\n    \n- SCIM filters should return filtered results\n    \n- Pagination should work with proper totalResults\n    \n- JSON Patch operations should update specific fields only\n    \n- Soft delete should mark records as inactive but not remove them\n    \n\n## 📝 Notes:\n\n- This collection uses real IDs from the test database\n    \n- All requests include proper Content-Type headers\n    \n- Test scripts validate response structure automatically\n    \n- The collection is ready for demonstration and production use",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "47263824",
